// CROWN — latency rides a GENERIC op parameter instantiated at a fn:
// `emit(x: a)` handed a performing closure, the arm calls it, the install
// under `with !E`. Expect E_EffectMismatch.
//
// Checked clean and ran at 7 through the pinned boot (measured 2026-09-23).
// The instance's positions have mixed variance — an op PARAMETER flows
// performer to handler — and the arm's call charges the handler's
// declaration-time residual, which the install never instantiates.
effect E { op() -> Int }
effect Emit { emit(x: a) -> Int }
fn loud() = op()
handler runit { emit(x) => resume(x()) }
fn bad() with !E = emit(loud) ~> runit
handler h { op() => resume(7) }
fn main() = bad() ~> h
